{{DASHBOARD_ROWS}}

*Derived* means computed from the three inputs with no unproved hypothesis; *selected* means an object (a pair, a grid cell, a chart) was chosen because it lands near the measured value, which counts as a fit; *conditional* means the value rests on a stated conjecture or an unproved step; *open* means the model does not yet reproduce the quantity. Two of the close agreements carry further qualifications: the fine-structure value is conditional on an open step in the Lean formalisation, and the kaon-to-pion ratio rests on a fusion pair chosen from a scan and includes a truncated correction series. The deuteron and helium-4 binding energies are the grid cell nearest the measured deuteron out of several few-body models and energy charts compared in the full scorecard. The ruled trace pipeline (a γγ-selected bond between the two nucleons, the tower energy scale and the logarithmic binding law) is shown beside them: it binds the deuteron by about $6\;\mathrm{keV}$, $99.7\%$ short. Beyond the lightest nuclei the binding energies come from a chain proxy whose saturation is open, and they fall short by a median of ${{BINDING_MEDIAN_PCT}}\%$. The $\beta$-decay values and the binding energies are the clearest places where the model, as it stands, does not yet work.
